id: pm-1tns7o
title: "The N-branch convergence property is proven only over the field class that cannot diverge: the randomized suite varies one union collection and compares it sorted"
description: "tests/fuzz/project-boundaries.fuzz.spec.ts:219 is the property that carries the convergence claim: 'converges randomized N-branch item appends independent of merge order'. It builds each branch by setting metadata.tags to a single generated tag, folds the branches with mergeItemDocuments in original and reversed order, and asserts converge(tags).sort() equals converge(reverse(tags)).sort(). Every element of that construction lands inside ITEM_UNION_COLLECTION_FIELDS, the eleven collections that merge by element identity and therefore cannot conflict; the assertion then sorts away even the ordering. No scalar field is varied, ours and theirs are never swapped, and the merged document is never compared as a whole. The conflict policy the merge actually implements — scalar three-way resolved toward the preferred side — has no convergence property at all. This is a gate-scope defect and is filed separately from the product behaviour it fails to cover, following the pm-wlqxg3/pm-m0yjtg precedent."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: convergence,gate,improve,merge,property-testing
created_at: "2026-08-02T21:05:06.550Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-11T14:44:13.242Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-11T14:44:12.658Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-11T14:44:12.658Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "The convergence property varies at least one scalar metadata field and the body in addition to union collections, and compares the whole merged document rather than a single field; The property asserts both application-order independence and merge-direction independence, exercising each branch pair as ours and as theirs; A deliberate regression that makes any union field direction-dependent, and a deliberate regression in the scalar path, each fail the suite; Every field class the merge distinguishes — union collection, latest-timestamp, scalar three-way — is named in the property and covered by at least one generated case, and adding a new field class without extending the property fails a conformance check"
value: A property suite that can only pass is not evidence; pm-2sbj8p names this suite as the acceptance evidence for the convergence model.
outcome: "The convergence property covers every field class the merge policy distinguishes, and a direction-dependent scalar fails it."
why_now: The ADR that must choose the convergence model is blocked on evidence this suite is supposed to supply.
parent: pm-33cw
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Replace tag-only convergence with independent whole-document conformance
expected_result: "Generated branch permutations and both directions preserve the independently specified scalar, body, union and timestamp outcomes"
actual_result: "Independent N-branch oracle passes; real union-loss, forced-direction and deterministic-description-loss source mutants fail; full 8724-test exact coverage and static quality pass"
